PeakPack optional patch (not in series by default).
Load Wine unixlibs with RTLD_GLOBAL so DXMT's winemetal.so can dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT, "macdrv_functions")
if G-A1 shows the symbol lookup failing (see DXMT issue #170). CrossOver's winemac.drv already
marks macdrv_functions DECLSPEC_EXPORT; this only changes symbol scope. Generated against CrossOver 26.3.0 sources/wine.
Apply with: patch -p1 -d src/wine < this file

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -1086,7 +1086,7 @@
     void *module, *handle;
     const IMAGE_NT_HEADERS *nt;
 
-    handle = dlopen( so_name, RTLD_NOW );
+    handle = dlopen( so_name, RTLD_NOW | RTLD_GLOBAL );
     if (!handle)
     {
         WARN( "failed to load .so lib %s: %s\n", debugstr_a(so_name), dlerror() );
